      "DDecision": "KEEP",
      "wholeDEENEquivalent": true,
      "scienceRationale": "Gene technology preserves DE Gentechnik: investigation by Gentest plus somatic gene addition and selected DNA cloning, not generic non-gene biotechnology or genome-editing-only. The same outline-level comparison is assessed in both languages; current title/description in native page/input are correct. Original A18 KEEP and genuine historical B broader-English HOLD remain preserved, and unrelated17 are not reopened.",
      "caseReview": [
        {
          "caseId": "he9-19-19-case-1",
          "decision": "PASS",
          "rationale": "A examines a selected DNA sequence, B adds a functional copy to selected body cells, C propagates a selected fragment in host cells. Full material/task/model-answer in both languages distinguish diagnostic investigation, somatic therapy and DNA cloning; no promised cure, germline change or cloned whole person."
        },
        {
          "caseId": "he9-19-19-case-2",
          "decision": "PASS",
          "rationale": "Intron-free coding DNA, appropriate vector/regulatory sequences, production-cell propagation and expression support the bounded recombinant protein model. Giving its protein to the recipient does not transfer a gene and thus is not the modelled gene therapy. DNA-fragment cloning differs from donor-organism cloning. This genuine contextual transfer is not merely repeating method names; no laboratory/clinical instruction or performance is asserted."
        }
      ],
